30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,The ledger shows fixed costs are high. The treasurer spent six hours a month chasing money.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The bank statements confirm it. A third of members needed reminders. We cannot rely on timely payment.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,The sign-up records show eleven mid-year joiners. Each needed a hand-worked calculation. That is a barrier.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The winter social notes are telling. Three quiet members said they feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The data is clear. Nine people do the work, eighteen pay for nothing. The current model is broken.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, yes. If we charge per visit, the treasurer spends all night calculating. We need a flat rate.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, a flat rate is risky. If attendance drops, we lose money. We need a base fee.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,A base fee plus a small per-visit charge might work. It keeps the entry low but covers costs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, that sounds fair. But if the per-visit charge is visible, it creates that hesitation I see.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,A base fee covers the core. The per-visit charge must be negligible to avoid the psychological barrier.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I prefer the base fee. It simplifies the books. The treasurer can just collect the same amount every month.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The base fee must be high enough to cover the seventy percent fixed costs. No more guessing.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I am concerned about the visibility. If the per-visit charge is on the receipt, it feels like a penalty.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,Exactly. The hesitation comes from the feeling of being charged for belonging. We must hide the variable part.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let’s make the base fee the main thing. The variable part should be a small, almost invisible adjustment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we have a path. A solid base fee, and a very small, simple variable part.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will support a structure that guarantees the fixed costs are covered. Stability is key.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will support a structure that keeps the entry point low and the process simple for newcomers.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I will support a structure that removes the sting of the per-visit charge. We need to feel like we belong.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I will support a structure that reflects the actual usage. The heavy users should carry a slightly larger share.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
