58,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A is the simplest. The treasurer only collects once. It is peaceful and clear.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is risky. If attendance drops, the fee is too low. We need to know the cost per head.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A is good for newcomers. No one sees a variable charge. It feels like a single, simple commitment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A removes the hesitation. You pay once, and you belong. There is no weighing up each evening.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is unfair. The eighteen who never come pay the same as the nine who do everything.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but the treasurer’s hours are the real cost. Option B means six hours a month of chasing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, I understand. But if the base fee in Option B is too low, we are back to guessing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,Option B creates that visible distinction. The receipt shows the extra charge. It feels like a penalty for coming.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, yes. The hesitation is exactly that. The feeling of being charged for the privilege of being there.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is the only one that acknowledges the difference. The heavy users choose the higher tier.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,Option C is complicated. The treasurer has to track who is in which tier. It adds to the burden.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is reasonable. The higher tier covers the fixed costs. The lower tier is for the occasional visitor.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,Option C creates a visible hierarchy. The named levels make the difference obvious. That is what I fear.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Option C is too cold. It labels people. I want everyone to feel they belong, not that they are in a class.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is rational. It matches the fee to the usage. The data shows the usage is not equal.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am leaning towards Option A. The simplicity is worth the risk. The treasurer needs rest.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I am leaning towards Option C. It provides the financial certainty I need. The higher tier covers the base.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am leaning towards Option A. It keeps the environment low-pressure. No one is singled out by a tier.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I am leaning towards Option A. It removes the hesitation. You pay, and you are part of the club.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am leaning towards Option C. It is the only one that is fair to the people who do the work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
